  "limitations": [
    "RenaissanceRe has nine semantically separate dollar rows in each of two filings, totalling 18/39 reference records. The macro-issuer score is reported separately.",
    "Travelers Q3/YTD incurred displays are repetitions of the same single-event incurred amount. Keeping current-quarter and year-to-date columns as separate opportunities would add one positive; estimated ultimate is always a separate source-labelled measure.",
    "Sign, ownership, tax/reinsurance scope, as-of date and column are part of semantic validation. Company-specific aggregate portfolio movements described as only principally related to Ian are excluded.",
    "Reference entries are filing-level and frequently economically overlap. Never sum them as an estimate of losses. All forms have at least one positive record, so a blank-form false-positive rate cannot be estimated here."
  ]
}
